===== kor --help
Kor: provider-agnostic, local-first coding agent

Usage: kor [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]... [COMMAND]

Commands:
  ask                 Ask one question and print the answer; attach images with --image
  resume              Continue a saved session (the latest if no id is given)
  sessions            List saved sessions
  completions         Shell completions (bash, zsh, fish, powershell, elvish, nushell)
  plan                Plans the agent saved in plan mode (`.kor/plans/`)
  status              Running tasks, pending approvals, daemon and remote tasks on this machine
  approve             Approve a pending request (desktop chat, daemon job or remote task)
  deny                Deny a pending request
  approvals           Approval queue: every pending request, one card at a time
  notifications       Notification center (same list as the desktop bell)
  integrate           "Open with Kor" right-click entries in the file manager and kor:// links
  files               Edit with Kor: apply one instruction to many files (preview, confirm, kor undo)
  folder              ~/Kor folder: sessions, images, reports, diffs and recordings as plain files
  mount               Mount the ~/Kor folder as a virtual drive (WebDAV, no driver to install)
  os-integration      Operating-system integrations (PowerToys Run, Windows Terminal, Shortcuts, GNOME, KDE…)
  host                Hosting panels and servers: connect, inventory, tasks (§29.1)
  wp                  WordPress/WooCommerce: inventory, health, plugin doctor, updates (§29.3–29.4)
  redirects           Redirect map for site migrations (§29.11)
  proposal            Client proposals and contracts (§29.12)
  client              Client workspaces and monthly report (§29.13)
  tr                  Turkey layer: KVKK, Turkish SEO, VAT, e-invoice, payments, marketplaces (§29.14)
  seo                 Technical SEO: audit, Search Console/GA4, content, bulk meta, logs, competitors, agent team, opportunities
  intents             Natural-language command routing: which sentence runs which command
  tool                Command-line tools on this computer and your typed tool definitions
  peer                Kor-to-Kor bridge: pair machines, delegate tasks, sync memory
  server              Self-hosted team server: set it up, add members, run it; join a team and sign in
  acp                 Agent Client Protocol: editors (Zed …) use Kor as their agent; other ACP agents run as sub-agents
  lsp                 Language server for editors (LSP on stdin/stdout): Kor diagnostics, explanations, code graph, tasks
  chrome              Kor browser extension: pairing, install, domain lists, form profiles
  computer            Desktop control: on/off and per-app permission tiers
  system              This machine's profile and health
  clean               Clean build and tool caches (`--suggest` lists them first)
  layout              Save and restore window arrangements across monitors
  prereq              System prerequisites only the OS can install (Docker/Podman, WSL2, Xcode tools, WebView2, macOS permissions)
  export              Export all user data into one archive (sessions, memory, knowledge base, audit log, settings)
  know                Search your personal knowledge base
  estimate            Time and cost estimate of a task before it runs
  rules               Check changes against the loaded rules
  docs                Private documents for the agent
  tui                 Open the full-screen terminal interface
  compat              Show what Kor reads from other AI coding tools' files (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Roo, Copilot, Gemini and more)
  trust               Trust this project: its own config may grant permissions, run hooks and set env
  doctor              Diagnose the local environment
  catalog             Model intelligence, speed, price and context data with sources (keyless, cached for 24 hours)
  hooks               Hooks run around edits, commands, commits and tasks
  media               Image, video and audio generation: capability catalog across providers, missing-parameter card, gallery and derivation chain, fal models; outputs under kor-media/
  hf                  Hugging Face: Hub search, model info, downloads and task inference
  agents              List the agents the Agent tool can start
  memory              Show this project's memory file
  recall              Search the knowledge base of earlier work in every project
  forget              Delete a knowledge base record
  knowledge           Knowledge base
  workspace           Folders of the multi-repo view
  graph               Live project graph: status and hotspots, or a subcommand (spec §7)
  db                  Database tables in the project graph: list, connect, refresh, show
  vault               Secret vault: named secrets in the OS keychain, given to agent commands as environment variables
  audit               Security/compliance analysis (--security, --compliance) and the hash-chained audit log
  sandbox             Command sandbox: backend, limits, network allowlist, self-test
  offline             Work without internet: local runtime, models, air-gap bundles
  task                Split a goal among parallel sub-agents, each in its own git worktree; review, merge and test the result
  pr                  Pull requests on GitHub, GitLab, Gitea/Forgejo and Bitbucket
  review              Review a diff with a persona (security, performance, rust-idiomatic, junior-friendly)
  daemon              Background process that runs triggers (§8.4)
  triggers            Event-driven tasks: git push, cron, webhook, log match
  deploy              Deploy changed services to an environment (compose, Kubernetes, Dockerfile)
  watch               Watch logs for errors and fix them with the agent
  find                Natural-language codebase search: relevant places with file:line and a plain-prose explanation of the flow (spec §8.9)
  deps                Dependencies: list, licenses, vulnerabilities, unused and upgrades
  explain             Code archaeology of a file: history, authors, renames, danger zones, graph; optional plain-language explanation (--level junior|normal|expert)
  quality             Project quality grade A–F per dimension with sources, improvement list and per-commit trend
  debt                Technical debt per file in estimated hours, monthly growth and threshold projection
  style               Measure your coding style and store it in the project memory
  stats               Your weekly developer statistics (human / agent lines, fixes, features, streak)
  impact              What a change to a file, symbol or diff affects, with an effort estimate
  dead-code           Unreachable code from entry points; --prune opens a verified removal PR
  screenshot          Turn a UI screenshot (or Figma PNG export) into components: React, Svelte, Tauri or HTML (spec §10)
  diagram             Turn an architecture diagram into a services/modules skeleton: interfaces and empty implementations (spec §10)
  visualize           Interactive architecture map, call graph and data flow from the project graph, without a model (spec §10)
  voice               Speak a task: records the microphone and transcribes it locally with whisper.cpp; no audio leaves the machine (spec §10)
  perf                Profile a command, the tests or an HTTP endpoint: flamegraph, hot functions mapped to the project graph, before/after
  replay              Replay recorded sessions: timeline, pause, step, diffs, export
  env                 Project environment (devcontainer, compose, nix, mise) and pinned tool versions
  remote-serve        Remote side of `kor --remote` (speaks JSON lines on stdin/stdout; started over SSH)
  attach              Follow a remote task again after a disconnect (with --remote); without a task, list them
  discover            Read-only scan of a server over SSH: services, ports, virtual hosts, cron, disks, languages
  packages            Monorepo packages: list, affected by changes, dependencies, cost
  connections         List SSH hosts and databases from connections.toml
  cost                Cost per model, this month and projection from the usage ledger (CLI and desktop)
  quota               Remaining provider quota per key, last 24 hours and failover order
  context             Context window breakdown of the last request, thresholds and recent use
  bench               Race models on your own test suite and suggest routing (.kor/bench.toml)
  shell               Shell integration: record the last failed command for kor fix / kor why
  fix                 Explain the last failed command and offer a corrected one
  why                 Explain why the last command failed
  consensus           Ask 2–3 models the same thing in parallel; keep the lines most agree on, show the rest
  comment             Translate code comments into a language; with --missing, write one-line comments for functions without one
  commit              Conventional Commits message from the staged changes
  fim                 Fill in the code at a cursor position with Mistral Codestral
  changelog           Keep a Changelog section from the commits since the last tag
  templates           Prompt and task templates (project, personal, plugin and built-in)
  run                 Run a task template through the agent: kor run template:<name> --<input> value
  routines            Scheduled tasks (the desktop app runs them while open)
  update              Check for, install or roll back a signed Kor release
  component           Downloadable helper programs: Python, Node, PDF renderer, OCR models, headless Chromium
  undo                Revert every file change of a session (the latest by default)
  auth                Manage provider API keys
  config              Inspect configuration
  providers           List known providers with their privacy tier and key status
  provider            Test, monitor and add model providers; manage the key pool
  proxy               Built-in CLIProxyAPI-compatible gateway: OpenAI, Anthropic and Gemini endpoints over your providers
  models              List models from the providers you have configured (cached for 24 hours)
  chrome-native-host  Chrome native messaging host (4-byte length prefix)
  mcp                 MCP servers: list, add (command, database, OpenAPI, GraphQL or folder), test, serve
  plugin              Plugin marketplaces and installs
  chat                Send one prompt and stream the reply (no tools)
  help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PROMPT]...
          Prompt to run once (omit for interactive mode)

Options:
      --lang <LANG>
          Interface language (tr, en, fr)

      --privacy-mode
          Privacy mode: local models only, no outbound calls from Kor

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

      --project <PROJECT>
          Project folder on the remote server (with --remote)

  -p, --print
          Print mode: run once, refuse anything that needs approval, print only the answer

      --json
          With -p: events as JSON lines (context.usage …)

  -m, --model <MODEL>
          Model as provider/model (overrides agent.model)

      --mode <MODE>
          Permission mode: default, plan, accept-edits, dont-ask, bypass-permissions or auto

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
===== kor ask --help
Ask one question and print the answer; attach images with --image

Usage: kor ask [OPTIONS] <QUESTION>...

