          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

  -h, --help
          Print help
===== kor sessions --help
List saved sessions

Usage: kor sessions [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  ls           List sessions (filter by tag, folder, pin)
  search       Search sessions by text (and by meaning with the local embedding model)
  mv           Move a session into a folder (no folder: out of it)
  pin          Pin a session (--off unpins)
  archive      Archive a session (--off restores)
  tag          Add tags to a session (--remove takes them off)
  color        Colour of a session: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple, gray or none
  rename       Set a session's title
  suggest      Suggest a title and tags (--apply saves them)
  export       Write every session as Markdown, one folder per session folder
  import       Read a Markdown export back as a session
  import-from  Import chats from Claude Code or Cursor (read only)
  fork         Fork a session after message N into a new session (its own git worktree)
  tree         A session's branches as a tree
  compare      Compare two branches: shared history, conclusions, file differences
  merge        Take a branch's conclusion back into its parent (files reviewed one by one)
  unfork       Forget a branch and remove its worktree (the transcript stays)
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --lang <LANG>
          Interface language (tr, en, fr)

      --tag <TAG>
          Only sessions with this tag

      --folder <FOLDER>
          Folder name

      --privacy-mode
          Privacy mode: local models only, no outbound calls from Kor

      --pinned
          Only pinned sessions

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

      --archived
          Include archived sessions

      --all
          All sessions, not only the newest 30

      --json
          Machine-readable JSON output

  -h, --help
          Print help
