===== kor peer --help
Kor-to-Kor bridge: pair machines, delegate tasks, sync memory

Usage: kor peer [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  pair     Show a pairing code (and QR) for another machine, or join one with --join
  list     Paired machines with their load and permissions
  serve    Answer paired machines (TCP, or stdin/stdout for SSH)
  run      Run a task on a paired machine; a copy of this project goes along
  attach   Follow a task on a machine again (no task: list them)
  result   Files a task changed, as a diff; --apply writes them here
  sync     Sync memory with a machine (three-way merge, both directions)
  allow    Set what a machine may do here (read-only by default)
  route    How to reach a machine: its SSH target and addresses
  remove   Forget a paired machine
  standby  Mirror the running session to a machine; if this one closes, it continues there
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --lang <LANG>
          Interface language (tr, en, fr)

      --privacy-mode
          Privacy mode: local models only, no outbound calls from Kor

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

  -h, --help
          Print help
