===== kor audit --help
Security/compliance analysis (--security, --compliance) and the hash-chained audit log

Usage: kor audit [OPTIONS]
       kor audit <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list           Show entries, newest first
  verify         Verify the hash chain
  report         Compliance report (KVKK/GDPR) built from the audit log
  export         Copy the audit log as JSON lines, with its verification result
  verify-report  Check an analysis report against the audit log and its signature
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --lang <LANG>
          Interface language (tr, en, fr)

      --privacy-mode
          Privacy mode: local models only, no outbound calls from Kor

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

      --security
          Security scan: secrets, injection, weak crypto, open endpoints, path traversal, TLS

      --compliance <kvkk|gdpr>
          Personal-data processing points (KVKK or GDPR)
          
          [possible values: kvkk, gdpr]

      --licenses
          Audit dependency licenses (SPDX) with the [audit.licenses] deny policy

      --path <PATH>
          Project root (default: current directory)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Report format: md, json or sarif
          
          [default: md]
          [possible values: md, json, sarif]

      --out <OUT>
          Write the report to this file

      --sign
          Record the report hash in the audit log; with a minisign key also write .minisig

      --min-severity <MIN_SEVERITY>
          Only findings at this severity or worse
          
          [possible values: critical, high, medium, low, info]

      --no-external
          Do not run gitleaks / semgrep even when installed

      --explain
          Ask the model to explain and fix the top findings

  -m, --model <MODEL>
          Model for this command (provider/model)

  -h, --help
          Print help
