===== kor task --help
Split a goal among parallel sub-agents, each in its own git worktree; review, merge and test the result

Usage: kor task [OPTIONS] [GOAL]...
       kor task <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list     Tasks of this repository
  status   Sub-agents of a task: role, model, status, cost, branch
  resume   Continue a stopped or crashed task from its checkpoint
  fork     Copy a task from the same point onto new branches
  cancel   Stop a task and remove its worktrees (the task branch stays)
  resolve  Settle a merge conflict: re-plan that part or drop it
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [GOAL]...
          What the team should do

Options:
      --lang <LANG>
          Interface language (tr, en, fr)

      --privacy-mode
          Privacy mode: local models only, no outbound calls from Kor

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

      --agents <AGENTS>
          Number of sub-agents (1–16)

      --model-per-role <MODEL_PER_ROLE>
          Pinned models per role: backend=openai/gpt-4.1,docs=local/qwen3

      --budget-usd <BUDGET_USD>
          Budget for the whole task in USD

      --orchestrator-model <ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL>
          Model that plans and re-plans

      --test <TEST>
          Test command run before review and on the merged branch (sandboxed)

      --parallel <PARALLEL>
          Sub-agents running at the same time

      --on <ON>
          Run the task on a paired machine (auto = the least busy)

  -h, --help
          Print help
