===== kor perf --help
Profile a command, the tests or an HTTP endpoint: flamegraph, hot functions mapped to the project graph, before/after

Usage: kor perf [OPTIONS] <TARGET>
       kor perf <COMMAND>

Commands:
  report  Read an existing profile file and map it to the project graph
  list    Earlier profiling runs of this project
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  <TARGET>
          A command (quoted), `test`, or an http(s) URL on this computer

Options:
      --lang <LANG>
          Interface language (tr, en, fr)

      --privacy-mode
          Privacy mode: local models only, no outbound calls from Kor

      --profiler <PROFILER>
          samply, perf, pprof, node, py-spy, cprofile, async-profiler, dotnet-trace or sample (default: by language)

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

      --duration <DURATION>
          Endpoint: seconds to sample the server (default 10). Command: time limit (default 600)

      --requests <REQUESTS>
          Endpoint: number of GET requests
          
          [default: 200]

      --concurrency <CONCURRENCY>
          Endpoint: requests at a time
          
          [default: 10]

      --pid <PID>
          Endpoint: process id of the running server to profile

      --cmd <SERVER_CMD>
          Endpoint: command that starts the server (Kor stops it afterwards)

      --allow-host <ALLOW_HOST>
          Endpoint: allow this non-loopback host for the load generator

      --optimize
          Let the agent change the hottest function (reviewed per file), then measure again and compare

      --out <OUT>
          Also write the flamegraph SVG here

      --yes
          Do not ask (also for running outside the sandbox)

  -h, --help
          Print help
