===== kor bench --help
Race models on your own test suite and suggest routing (.kor/bench.toml)

Usage: kor bench [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --file <FILE>
          Bench spec file (default: .kor/bench.toml)

      --lang <LANG>
          Interface language (tr, en, fr)

  -m, --model <MODELS>
          Model to race (provider/model); repeatable, replaces the spec's list

      --privacy-mode
          Privacy mode: local models only, no outbound calls from Kor

      --max-cost <MAX_COST>
          Do not start above this estimated cost in USD without --yes
          
          [default: 0.5]

      --remote <REMOTE>
          Run the agent on this server over SSH: user@host[:port] or a connections.toml id

  -y, --yes
          Start even when the estimate is above --max-cost or a price is unknown

      --json <JSON>
          Also write the full report as JSON to this file ("-" for standard output)

      --baseline <BASELINE>
          Router comparison: run every task on this model, then again with routing

      --route <ROUTES>
          Route for the comparison as category=provider/model; repeatable

      --graph [<GRAPH>]
          Graph tools off vs on: on or off runs one arm, bare --graph runs both and compares tokens
          
          [possible values: on, off, both]

      --ui
          Measure the TUI and desktop budgets (§32.1)

      --cli
          Measure the CLI budgets: start-up, token path, idle memory and CPU, binary size, soak

      --memory
          Measure the knowledge base budgets (§31.3.1)

      --history <HISTORY>
          Benchmark history file
          
          [default: bench/history.json]

      --record
          Append this run to the history

      --check
          Fail when a budget is exceeded or a measurement is more than 5% slower than the baseline

      --update-baseline
          Make this run the baseline of this machine

      --weak
          Weak CI worker (2 cores / 4 GB): budgets relaxed ×2

      --desktop <DESKTOP>
          Path of the kor-desktop binary (default: KOR_DESKTOP or next to kor)

      --records <RECORDS>
          Knowledge base records for --memory
          
          [default: 1000000]

      --performance-md <PERFORMANCE_MD>
          Write PERFORMANCE.md (weekly charts) from the history

  -h, --help
          Print help
