===== kor provider --help
Test, monitor and add model providers; manage the key pool

Usage: kor provider [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  test        List a provider's models, then make one tiny streaming call and report latency
  status      Latency, error rate and remaining quota per provider
  add         Add an OpenAI- or Anthropic-compatible endpoint, a local server or a subscription proxy (cliproxy)
  remove      Remove a provider added with `kor provider add`
  discover    Find local model servers (Ollama, vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio, Jan, LocalAI, text-generation-webui, KoboldCpp) on their default ports
  keys        Show the keys in a provider's failover pool (masked)
  add-key     Store one more key for a provider; on 429, 5xx or a timeout Kor switches to the next key
  remove-key  Delete the key in one pool slot
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

